WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.910
An open-air stage around
1600, the crowd standing.

2
00:00:04.960 --> 00:00:09.350
Beside it, a modern theatre,
rows of seats in the dark.

3
00:00:09.400 --> 00:00:13.790
On both stages, the same robed
figure speaks the same lines:

4
00:00:13.840 --> 00:00:16.090
"Hath not a Jew eyes?"

5
00:00:16.140 --> 00:00:19.290
He lists what he shares with
the Christians around him:

6
00:00:19.340 --> 00:00:23.280
"hands, organs, dimensions, senses".

7
00:00:23.330 --> 00:00:26.270
Four centuries apart, one speech.

8
00:00:26.320 --> 00:00:29.520
So why does the play
land so differently now?

9
00:00:29.570 --> 00:00:33.270
In this mission, you'll ask what
has changed in four centuries:

10
00:00:33.320 --> 00:00:35.810
the words, or the people hearing them?

11
00:00:35.860 --> 00:00:39.930
You'll read Shylock's speech
closely, from Act 3, Scene 1.

12
00:00:39.980 --> 00:00:44.130
And you'll watch a novel's first
reviewers and its later readers clash,

13
00:00:44.180 --> 00:00:47.560
over Jane Eyre, published in 1847.

14
00:00:47.610 --> 00:00:51.980
Your mission: explain why the
same play lands differently today.
